{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Prob_the_fastest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Prob the fastest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure below, each circle will be filled with a digit from 1 to 6. Each digit must appear exactly once. The sum of the digits in neighboring circles is shown in the box between them. What digit must be placed in the top circle?\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q12.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/fe/2026_amc_8_q12.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"415\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e8570e76bf7aad746c0cbd204b47e84fec253871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 3\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 5\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\text{it is impossible to fill the circles}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"578\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote an odd number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote an even. Then, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a4d27a04488af692e4d5ad91c21a810014a110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O+E = O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />, and thus the two neighboring circles that form sums 9 and 5 must be one of each odd and even. To obtain 5, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba3011c19ad23c26405df20cfad723dd8725777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0caf2babfb6bba9b38a08a9ff7deb6164762f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. To obtain 9, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/1067acb571cf793276184f650bba767d064cfc7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e270eec110c1fe309a69d93f34587e0e64aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Consider each case separately.\n</p><p>Case 1: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba3011c19ad23c26405df20cfad723dd8725777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> makes the sum of 5, then the two numbers that make 9 must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/1067acb571cf793276184f650bba767d064cfc7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Then, 3 is forced on top, and we require another 3. However, the problem doesn't allow this, so this is impossible.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0caf2babfb6bba9b38a08a9ff7deb6164762f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> is on 5, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e270eec110c1fe309a69d93f34587e0e64aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is on 9. Then, we have two subcases.\n</p><p>Case A: 4 is on top. Then, we require 2 to complete the sum of 6, which is not possible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0caf2babfb6bba9b38a08a9ff7deb6164762f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> is on 5.\n</p><p>Case B: 5 is on top, meaning that we require 1 right below, 3 on the bottom right, 2 to complete the sum of 5, and the rest are uniquely determined.\n</p><p>The number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897a203bdf45af36f2b9edc59c3bc0beeb898be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the bottom-left corner, we have 2 numbers that add up to 10 filled in from the digits from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are two ways you can do this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since we can only use each integer once, the first case doesn't work, so we must have the second case. Now we need to figure out the ordering. If we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the other circle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but again, we can only use each positive integer once, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that we can already find the number that needs to go into the circle we want, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e505661def97a84886192de38756eeb2833e505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697feca548bd97662d29974e67463bcdbe531535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-4=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. ~Baihly2024\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We do trial and error, and because it is a shorter problem it doesn’t take long. we can find that the only possibility is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e505661def97a84886192de38756eeb2833e505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />。\n</p><p>~pereena\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Prob_the_fastest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Prob_the_fastest)\">Solution 4 (Prob the fastest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Prob the fastest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set space 1 to the top, space 2 to the middle left, space 3 to the middle right, space 4 to the bottom left, space 5  to the bottom middle, and space 6 to the bottom right. Note that I am only doing this to better explain this to you, the numbering of spaces is just a waste of time on the AMC 8.\n</p><p>Look at space 3 and space 6. The numbers must sum to 4. The two numbers cannot be 2 and 2, as each digit must repeat only once, therefore the only number pair that satisfies this is 1 and 3. Now we must figure out where to place these numbers. We can now look at space 1 and space 3. If we say that space 3 is equal to 1, then space 1 must be equal to 5. That is one possible solution. Now, if we made space 3 equal to 3 instead, space 1 must be equal to 3 as well, which contradicts the problem. Therefore, the only possible solution is 5. Now, we must check and solve the rest of the triangle to make sure that there is a solution, and the answer is not E. We can now find that the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e505661def97a84886192de38756eeb2833e505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~apmathematician\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UTftrI4GYYg\">https://youtu.be/UTftrI4GYYg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1188s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1188s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qual